@page
@model Portal.Pages.TrafficModel

<partial name="_PageHead" model="@(new PageHeadModel(
    "Traffic",
    "Every proxy decision, joined to the ruleset that governs the workload that made it."))" />

@*
    Everything a filter changes lives in one region, because a filter changes what every panel
    shows. The filter controls hx-get this address with hx-push-url, and hx-select pulls this same
    region back out of the response — so the filtered view is a real URL, reachable by the back
    button and pasteable into a ticket.

    The mockup carries its freshness stamp in the page head. Here each panel refreshes on its own
    60-second trigger, so each carries its own stamp instead: one stamp above panels that update
    independently would be describing whichever of them refreshed last.
*@
<div id="traffic-results">
    <partial name="_TrafficFilters" model="Model" />
    <partial name="_TrafficSummary" model="Model" />
    <partial name="_TrafficDenials" model="Model" />

    <div class="grid g2">
        <partial name="_TrafficCredentials" model="Model" />
        <partial name="_TrafficChallenges" model="Model" />
    </div>

    <partial name="_TrafficVolume" model="Model" />
</div>
